#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Build research/amm-multi-hop-split-boost-tf-boost-trade-chains-20261029 receipts.

3rd run packet #102: the split x boost x tf chain at TRUE 3 hops
(three_amm only, final output U3 -- the route 3rd #63/#64 pinned)
meets boost-trade interaction both ways: a boost first and then a
trade (does the burn move the next price?), and a trade first and
then a boost (does the trade move the next burn?), plus alternation
sequences, failed-step recovery, bucket/buyback/claim interaction,
transfer-fee variation, and boost-size variation. All cases are
expected to agree on all three images; error sites are pinned per
image, never compared across images.

Route check (read from this builder, not the packet name):
build_route calls three_amm only and appends NO g4/g5 hop group,
so the route is main -> POOL2 -> P3, final output U3: TRUE 3 hops.
The quote mint carries a per-case transfer-fee config (bps 0/100/5000)
and the split legs route the buyback through the TOKEN22 ATA.
"""
